## ⚖️ 5. LEGAL CONSEQUENCES OF VIOLATION

### 5.1 Civil Penalties

**Violation of this license may result in:**

#### A. **Monetary Damages** 💰

- **Actual Damages**: Full financial losses incurred by DrishtiX
- **Statutory Damages**: Up to **$150,000 per work infringed** (17 U.S.C. § 504)
- **Treble Damages**: Up to **3x actual damages** for willful infringement
- **Lost Profits**: All profits derived from unauthorized use
- **Attorney's Fees**: Reimbursement of all legal costs (17 U.S.C. § 505)

#### B. **Injunctive Relief** 🛑

- **Immediate Cease & Desist**: Court-ordered termination of use
- **Permanent Injunction**: Prohibition from future use
- **Asset Seizure**: Confiscation of all unauthorized copies
- **Account Suspension**: Termination of GitHub, cloud, and related accounts

### 5.2 Criminal Penalties

**Unauthorized use may constitute criminal offenses:**

#### A. **Federal Crimes (United States)**

- **Copyright Infringement** (18 U.S.C. § 2319)
  - Fines up to **$250,000**
  - Imprisonment up to **5 years** (first offense)
  - Imprisonment up to **10 years** (repeat offenses)

- **Trade Secret Theft** (18 U.S.C. § 1832)
  - Fines up to **$5,000,000** (organizations)
  - Imprisonment up to **10 years**

- **Computer Fraud & Abuse** (18 U.S.C. § 1030)
  - Fines up to **$500,000**
  - Imprisonment up to **20 years** (if bodily harm results)

#### B. **State Crimes**

- Theft of Trade Secrets (varies by state)
- Fraud (varies by state)
- Misappropriation (varies by state)

### 5.3 International Enforcement

**This license is enforceable worldwide through:**

- WIPO Arbitration and Mediation Center
- International copyright treaties
- Bilateral enforcement agreements
- Local courts in violator's jurisdiction

### 5.4 Detection & Enforcement

**DrishtiX employs multiple detection mechanisms:**

- Code fingerprinting and watermarking
- Telemetry and usage tracking
- GitHub repository monitoring
- Search engine monitoring for unauthorized hosting
- Anonymous tip hotline
- Periodic audits of licensed users

**Violators WILL be prosecuted to the fullest extent of the law.**

